{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow tax-free salary sacrifice for fertility treatment and egg/sperm freezing",
        "additional_details": "Fertility challenges affect 1 in 7 UK couples, alongside same-sex couples and single individuals. Funding via the NHS can be limited, and private IVF or egg/sperm freezing can cost \u00a35,000\u2013\u00a310,000+. We believe that if this was tax-free, more people could use bonuses for private care, significantly relieving NHS pressure. Currently, the only way to divert bonuses pre-tax is into pensions. We call on the government to allow pre-tax salary sacrifice for fertility treatments and testing to remove financial barriers and give everyone a fair chance to build a family.",
        "background": "Government to allow individuals to pay for private fertility treatments, including IVF, egg/sperm freezing, and testing via tax-exempt Salary Sacrifice. The Treasury should classify reproductive care as an exempt workplace benefit, removing what can be a massive financial barrier.",
        "closed_at": null,
